      "title": "National Security Agency network for internal communications goes down",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/17/nsa-national-security-classified-communications-network-down",
      "description": "<p>NSA issues ‘code yellow’ as NSANet, used by staff to share classified material, including top-secret intelligence, fails</p><p>The National Security Agency said on Tuesday that it had experienced “temporary degradation” during scheduled routine maintenance, after reports that its classified internal communications network had gone down.</p><p>In a statement, the agency said some internal systems were affected but that “mission-critical capabilities remain fully operational” and its ability to defend national security continues. It said its infrastructure is built with “multiple layers of redundancy” to keep operations running during planned maintenance or unexpected events.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/17/nsa-national-security-classified-communications-network-down\">Continue reading...</a>",
